::: {.doc-subject}

Get a node object by ID or label.
:::

::: {.doc-usage-source}
Usage

[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L2824-L2863){target="_blank" rel="noopener"}
:::

::: {.doc-signature .doc-Kind.FUNCTION}
```python
Graph.get_node(node)
```
:::

::: {.doc-text}

Retrieves the `Node` object for the specified node. The `Node` object contains `id`,
`label`, and attributes properties. Returns `None` if node doesn't exist.
:::

## Parameters {.doc-parameters}

::: {.doc-definition-items}
<code>[node]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Union[int, str]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>

:   Node ID (str) or internal ID (int) to retrieve.
:::

## Returns {.doc-returns}

::: {.doc-definition-items}
<code> [Node | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>

:   `Node` object or `None` if not found.
:::

## Examples {.doc-examples}

Access node properties:

::: {#0f4eabeb .cell execution_count=1}
``` {.python .cell-code}
import edgecase as ec

graph = ec.Graph().add_node(label="A", color="red", size=10)

node = graph.get_node("A")

# Returns 'A'
node.id
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}
```
1
```
:::
:::


::: {#4cc5e49e .cell execution_count=2}
``` {.python .cell-code}
# Returns {'color': 'red', 'size': 10}
node.attributes
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}
```
{'color': 'red', 'size': 10}
```
:::
:::
